\f1\fs26 A snap of the fingers made the silence black.\
Less than a second later, when Cracker\'92s eyes started working again, the hallway wall cracked and toppled, like a truck hit it from the other side. Sarah pulled cracker to the floor as the blank compression of the blast receded and left his ears ringing. The ceiling buckled, ruptured, and spewed chips and splinters and chunks down. Sarah grunted out the grey dark and slumped. Grey lumpy icing sugar dusted Sarah\'92s hair and caked in her blood. Too late, Cracker, crouched over as the asteroid shower out of the ceiling slowed.\
Cracker assessed the space; the toppling wall\'92s complete collapse had been arrested by the other, still resolutely bearing the load of who-knows-what above it, forming a narrow triangular crawlspace around them. Cracker doubted it would hold long.\
\'93Sarah!\'94 Cracker slapped both her cheeks. There was no rousing her.\
The sound of falling chunks subsided, replaced by moans and wails.\
On his feet, crouching under the low lean-to of the toppled wall, Cracker hooped his arms under Sarah\'92s, and shuffled backwards, hoping the lobby of the club provided some form of escape. There was a 
\f2\i whomp
\f1\i0 , like a gas burner igniting. Swirling orange flared around and past him. The muted sounds of screams bloomed. Some of the screams were Cracker\'92s.
